00:10:38,136 --> 00:10:40,773
only about ten percent of owners drove

283
00:10:40,773 --> 00:10:42,230
their cars regularly.

284
00:10:42,410 --> 00:10:44,645
That is the other half of the

285
00:10:44,645 --> 00:10:47,496
bubble story: cars bought to be kept,

286
00:10:47,496 --> 00:10:48,343
not driven.

287
00:10:48,523 --> 00:10:49,941
Lee Iacocca's car,

288
00:10:49,941 --> 00:10:51,675
according to Autopian,

289
00:10:51,675 --> 00:10:55,536
covered sixty-five miles between two thousand six

290
00:10:55,536 --> 00:10:56,955
and twenty twelve,

291
00:10:56,955 --> 00:10:59,713
which is about eleven miles a year,

292
00:10:59,713 --> 00:11:01,131
by our arithmetic.

293
00:11:01,481 --> 00:11:03,441
The car that was born from a

294
00:11:03,441 --> 00:11:06,381
cancelled racing category did get to race.

295
00:11:06,561 --> 00:11:08,936
Wikipedia says the F forty L M

296
00:11:08,936 --> 00:11:12,023
debuted at Laguna Seca on the fifteenth

297
00:11:12,023 --> 00:11:14,635
of October, nineteen eighty-nine,

298
00:11:14,635 --> 00:11:16,139
and finished third.

299
00:11:16,319 --> 00:11:20,220
Ten Competizione-specification cars were built,

300
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:22,792
two L M and eight Competizione,

301
00:11:22,792 --> 00:11:25,282
with seven hundred horsepower.

302
00:11:25,462 --> 00:11:26,320
The G T E,

303
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:29,322
with six hundred twenty horsepower,

304
00:11:29,322 --> 00:11:30,094
followed.

305
00:11:30,444 --> 00:11:32,639
Seven G T E cars were built,

306
00:11:32,639 --> 00:11:35,538
Wikipedia says, and they won the four

307
00:11:35,538 --> 00:11:39,222
hours of Anderstorp in nineteen ninety-five and

308
00:11:39,222 --> 00:11:40,789
nineteen ninety-six.

309
00:11:40,969 --> 00:11:44,545
In all, nineteen racing cars were built.

310
00:11:44,725 --> 00:11:45,990
By our arithmetic,

311
00:11:45,990 --> 00:11:47,959
that is about one and a half

312
00:11:47,959 --> 00:11:49,787
percent of the production.

313
00:11:49,967 --> 00:11:52,403
A road car designed for a category

314
00:11:52,403 --> 00:11:55,841
that vanished eventually found racing elsewhere.

315
00:11:56,191 --> 00:11:58,220
The most valuable of them,

316
00:11:58,220 --> 00:12:01,575
per Sotheby's, is a nineteen ninety-three F

317
00:12:01,575 --> 00:12:03,448
forty L M by Michelotto.

318
00:12:03,628 --> 00:12:05,486
It sold for eleven million,

319
00:12:05,486 --> 00:12:08,996
five thousand dollars in August twenty twenty-five,

320
00:12:08,996 --> 00:12:11,474
and it has about seven hundred sixty

321
00:12:11,474 --> 00:12:12,231
horsepower.

322
00:12:12,411 --> 00:12:15,389
Sotheby's says it is one of nineteen

323
00:12:15,389 --> 00:12:17,043
Michelotto examples.

324
00:12:17,223 --> 00:12:18,718
The racing version,

325
00:12:18,718 --> 00:12:20,369
which Enzo never saw,

326
00:12:20,369 --> 00:12:22,886
now sets the price record in our

327
00:12:22,886 --> 00:12:23,516
sources.

328
00:12:23,865 --> 00:12:27,060
Classic Motorsports tracks the price after the

329
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:27,546
bubble.

330
00:12:27,726 --> 00:12:31,464
About one million dollars in twenty nineteen.

331
00:12:31,644 --> 00:12:33,646
A Mecum sale at two and a

332
00:12:33,646 --> 00:12:36,370
half million in twenty twenty-two.

333
00:12:36,550 --> 00:12:39,897
Around four million in twenty twenty-three,

334
00:12:39,897 --> 00:12:40,520
it says.

335
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:42,129
By our arithmetic,

336
00:12:42,129 --> 00:12:44,589
that is a fourfold rise in four

337
00:12:44,589 --> 00:12:45,065
years.

338
00:12:45,245 --> 00:12:47,547
The car that once lost nearly half

339
00:12:47,547 --> 00:12:49,712
its value in pounds had become a

340
00:12:49,712 --> 00:12:51,201
blue-chip collectible.

341
00:12:51,551 --> 00:12:55,011
Sotheby's lists the sales of twenty twenty-five.

342
00:12:55,191 --> 00:12:57,873
Alain Prost's nineteen ninety car,

343
00:12:57,873 --> 00:13:01,739
three million, eight hundred eighty-six thousand,

344
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:03,790
two hundred fifty dollars,

345
00:13:03,790 --> 00:13:05,210
with two thousand,

346
00:13:05,210 --> 00:13:07,498
nine hundred sixty-one miles.

347
00:13:07,678 --> 00:13:09,858
A nineteen ninety storage car,

348
00:13:09,858 --> 00:13:14,001
three million, eight hundred fifty-five thousand dollars,

349
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:16,618
with three hundred sixty kilometres.

350
00:13:16,798 --> 00:13:18,777
A U S-specification car,

351
00:13:18,777 --> 00:13:23,067
three million, five hundred eighty thousand dollars.

352
00:13:23,416 --> 00:13:25,765
A Swiss car sold for two million,

353
00:13:25,765 --> 00:13:28,185
nine hundred fifty-eight thousand,

354
00:13:28,185 --> 00:13:30,391
one hundred twenty-five francs,

355
00:13:30,391 --> 00:13:32,882
and a restored car for two million,

356
00:13:32,882 --> 00:13:35,230
eight hundred seventeen thousand,

357
00:13:35,230 --> 00:13:36,582
five hundred euros.

358
00:13:36,762 --> 00:13:39,985
Autopian reports a nineteen ninety-two car at

359
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:43,495
five million, two hundred thirty thousand dollars

360
00:13:43,495 --> 00:13:45,644
in February twenty twenty-six.

361
00:13:45,824 --> 00:13:47,706
These are separate sales,

362
00:13:47,706 --> 00:13:48,684
not an index,

363
00:13:48,684 --> 00:13:50,340
and the range is wide.

364
00:13:50,690 --> 00:13:52,012
By our arithmetic,

365
00:13:52,012 --> 00:13:54,361
the Prost sale is about nine and

366
00:13:54,361 --> 00:13:57,592
three-quarter times the launch price of four

367
00:13:57,592 --> 00:13:59,427
hundred thousand dollars,

368
00:13:59,427 --> 00:14:00,675
in nominal terms.

369
00:14:00,855 --> 00:14:04,176
The ModaMiami sale is about thirteen times.

370
00:14:04,356 --> 00:14:07,661
Those multiples are not adjusted for inflation,

371
00:14:07,661 --> 00:14:10,827
because our sources give no inflation figure,

372
00:14:10,827 --> 00:14:12,796
and the comparison is rough.

373
00:14:12,976 --> 00:14:15,844
Still, the direction is unmistakable.

374
00:14:16,193 --> 00:14:18,523
Owners do not just buy the story;

375
00:14:18,523 --> 00:14:19,723
they maintain it.

376
00:14:19,903 --> 00:14:23,443
Classic Motorsports says the belts are replaced

377
00:14:23,443 --> 00:14:24,799
every three years,

378
00:14:24,799 --> 00:14:27,210
with the engine in place but the

379
00:14:27,210 --> 00:14:29,620
seats and rear firewall removed.

380
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,680
Fluids are changed yearly,

381
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:33,922
for about one thousand dollars.

382
00:14:34,102 --> 00:14:37,185
Fuel bladders can leak after about ten

383
00:14:37,185 --> 00:14:40,105
years, though U S cars had aluminium

384
00:14:40,105 --> 00:14:40,592
tanks.

385
00:14:40,772 --> 00:14:42,879
It calls the car cheaper to run

386
00:14:42,879 --> 00:14:44,034
than the F fifty.

387
00:14:44,384 --> 00:14:47,843
Autopian itemised a preparation bill for Lee

388
00:14:47,843 --> 00:14:50,516
Iacocca's nineteen ninety-one car,

389
00:14:50,516 --> 00:14:53,503
chassis eighty-seven three forty-five,

390
00:14:53,503 --> 00:14:56,961
before a Monterey sale in twenty twenty-six:

391
00:14:56,961 --> 00:14:59,477
a coolant tank at four thousand,

392
00:14:59,477 --> 00:15:01,992
four hundred twenty-six dollars,

393
00:15:01,992 --> 00:15:05,529
engine service of nearly twenty-one thousand,

394
00:15:05,529 --> 00:15:07,259
tyres at two thousand,

395
00:15:07,259 --> 00:15:10,874
six hundred thirty-seven and a headlamp switch

396
00:15:10,874 --> 00:15:12,211
at four thousand,

397
00:15:12,211 --> 00:15:13,154
two hundred.

398
00:15:13,334 --> 00:15:16,271
About thirty-four thousand dollars in all.

399
00:15:16,621 --> 00:15:18,653
That article is inconsistent.

400
00:15:18,833 --> 00:15:21,853
Its headline says sixty thousand dollars and

401
00:15:21,853 --> 00:15:23,844
its body says forty thousand,

402
00:15:23,844 --> 00:15:25,972
while the items add up to about

403
00:15:25,972 --> 00:15:27,413
thirty-four thousand.

404
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:29,145
We cannot resolve it,

405
00:15:29,145 --> 00:15:31,436
so we use the itemised figures.

406
00:15:31,616 --> 00:15:33,321
It is a good example of how

407
00:15:33,321 --> 00:15:35,151
a story about this car can be

408
00:15:35,151 --> 00:15:37,172
repeated with the wrong numbers,

409
00:15:37,172 --> 00:15:39,318
which is why we keep showing where

410
00:15:39,318 --> 00:15:40,265
ours come from.

411
00:15:40,616 --> 00:15:43,030
Return for a moment to the Evoluzione.

412
00:15:43,210 --> 00:15:46,473
Five cars were built and never raced.

413
00:15:46,653 --> 00:15:49,324
Wikipedia does not say what happened to

414
00:15:49,324 --> 00:15:52,133
them afterwards, and neither do our other

415
00:15:52,133 --> 00:15:54,188
sources, so we will not guess.

416
00:15:54,368 --> 00:15:56,321
What we can say is that the

417
00:15:56,321 --> 00:15:59,070
project to turn that experiment into a

418
00:15:59,070 --> 00:16:01,386
road car started on the tenth of

419
00:16:01,386 --> 00:16:03,267
June, nineteen eighty-six,

420
00:16:03,267 --> 00:16:06,233
and ended with an unveiling in Maranello.

421
00:16:06,582 --> 00:16:08,848
It is worth pausing on how short

422
00:16:08,848 --> 00:16:10,193
thirteen months is.

423
00:16:10,373 --> 00:16:11,475
By our arithmetic,

424
00:16:11,475 --> 00:16:13,861
that is about three hundred ninety days

425
00:16:13,861 --> 00:16:16,064
between the start of the project and

426
00:16:16,064 --> 00:16:16,921
the unveiling.

427
00:16:17,101 --> 00:16:18,563
Compare the Porsche,

428
00:16:18,563 --> 00:16:22,216
which Wikipedia says took from nineteen eighty-one

429
00:16:22,216 --> 00:16:25,066
to deliveries in nineteen eighty-seven,

430
00:16:25,066 --> 00:16:27,550
about six years by our arithmetic.

431
00:16:27,730 --> 00:16:30,336
The Ferrari took roughly one sixth of

432
00:16:30,336 --> 00:16:30,969
the time.

433
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:33,136
The reason, by our reading,

434
00:16:33,136 --> 00:16:35,154
is that the Ferrari had a head

435
00:16:35,154 --> 00:16:35,557
start.

436
00:16:35,737 --> 00:16:37,211
The Evoluzione existed,

437
00:16:37,211 --> 00:16:39,069
and so did the engine family.

438
00:16:39,249 --> 00:16:41,589
Our sources do not say which parts

439
00:16:41,589 --> 00:16:43,723
carried over, so we do not list

440
00:16:43,723 --> 00:16:44,067
them.

441
00:16:44,247 --> 00:16:46,245
They say only that the F forty

442
00:16:46,245 --> 00:16:48,575
grew out of the Evoluzione and that

443
00:16:48,575 --> 00:16:50,772
the project took thirteen months.

444
00:16:50,952 --> 00:16:52,398
The rest is inference,

445
00:16:52,398 --> 00:16:54,040
and we label it that way.

446
00:16:54,391 --> 00:16:56,180
The F forty is a car of

447
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:59,370
disputed numbers, and the dispute is part

448
00:16:59,370 --> 00:17:00,381
of its story.

449
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:03,573
Wikipedia lists its weight at one thousand,

450
00:17:03,573 --> 00:17:06,865
two hundred fifty-four kilograms for Europe and

451
00:17:06,865 --> 00:17:10,088
one thousand, three hundred sixty-nine for the

452
00:17:10,088 --> 00:17:11,068
United States.

453
00:17:11,248 --> 00:17:14,957
The DK Engineering archive says one thousand,

454
00:17:14,957 --> 00:17:16,275
two hundred two.

455
00:17:16,455 --> 00:17:17,784
By our arithmetic,

456
00:17:17,784 --> 00:17:20,589
the gap between the lowest and highest

457
00:17:20,589 --> 00:17:23,837
figure is one hundred sixty-seven kilograms,

458
00:17:23,837 --> 00:17:26,347
about thirteen and a half percent.

459
00:17:26,698 --> 00:17:28,938
The power figures differ as well.

460
00:17:29,118 --> 00:17:33,528
Wikipedia says four hundred seventy-eight metric horsepower,

461
00:17:33,528 --> 00:17:36,320
and four hundred eighty-four for the U

462
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:36,467
S.

463
00:17:36,647 --> 00:17:39,812
The DK Engineering archive says about five

464
00:17:39,812 --> 00:17:42,901
hundred brake horsepower at one point one

465
00:17:42,901 --> 00:17:43,880
bar of boost.

466
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:46,563
Our sources do not reconcile these,

467
00:17:46,563 --> 00:17:48,135
so we report them all.

468
00:17:48,315 --> 00:17:49,737
In a car this famous,

469
00:17:49,737 --> 00:17:52,782
even the basic specification depends on which

470
00:17:52,782 --> 00:17:53,865
source you open.

471
00:17:54,215 --> 00:17:56,560
The emissions equipment differs too.

472
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:59,369
Wikipedia says the early cars had no

473
00:17:59,369 --> 00:18:02,510
catalytic converters until nineteen ninety.

474
00:18:02,690 --> 00:18:05,822
The DK Engineering archive says they arrived

475
00:18:05,822 --> 00:18:07,601
from nineteen ninety-one.

476
00:18:07,781 --> 00:18:08,763
One year apart,

477
00:18:08,763 --> 00:18:10,925
but a collector will tell you the

478
00:18:10,925 --> 00:18:12,169
difference matters.

479
00:18:12,349 --> 00:18:14,205
We do not know which is right,

480
00:18:14,205 --> 00:18:15,751
and we do not pretend to.

481
00:18:15,931 --> 00:18:16,814
We note it,

482
00:18:16,814 --> 00:18:17,777
and move on.

483
00:18:18,128 --> 00:18:20,241
Behind the car were several people.

484
00:18:20,421 --> 00:18:22,952
Nicola Materazzi, who proposed it.

485
00:18:23,132 --> 00:18:26,091
Pietro Camardella and Aldo Brovarone,

486
00:18:26,091 --> 00:18:28,971
who shaped the body for Pininfarina.

487
00:18:29,151 --> 00:18:31,264
Enzo Ferrari, who approved it.

488
00:18:31,444 --> 00:18:34,016
Our sources give no more detail about

489
00:18:34,016 --> 00:18:36,031
their roles, so we do not add

490
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:36,309
any.

491
00:18:36,489 --> 00:18:39,104
A common mistake in retellings is to

492
00:18:39,104 --> 00:18:41,574
credit one person with everything.

493
00:18:41,754 --> 00:18:43,832
The sources point to a team.

494
00:18:44,183 --> 00:18:46,713
Then there were the drivers and owners

495
00:18:46,713 --> 00:18:48,977
who gave the car its famous names.

496
00:18:49,157 --> 00:18:52,389
Alain Prost, whose nineteen ninety car sold

497
00:18:52,389 --> 00:18:54,719
in December twenty twenty-five.

498
00:18:54,899 --> 00:18:57,737
Nigel Mansell, whose car was sold in

499
00:18:57,737 --> 00:19:01,284
nineteen ninety and again in twenty fourteen.

500
00:19:01,464 --> 00:19:05,069
Lee Iacocca, whose nineteen ninety-one car was

501
00:19:05,069 --> 00:19:06,480
ordered in Modena.

502
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:08,921
Our sources do not say how they

503
00:19:08,921 --> 00:19:10,016
drove the cars,

504
00:19:10,016 --> 00:19:12,058
only how the cars were sold.

505
00:19:12,409 --> 00:19:14,159
And the Sultan of Brunei,

506
00:19:14,159 --> 00:19:17,240
who according to Wikipedia received at least

507
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:19,200
seven right-hand-drive cars.

508
00:19:19,380 --> 00:19:21,695
Beyond that, the page says nothing about

509
00:19:21,695 --> 00:19:22,968
what he did with them.

510
00:19:23,148 --> 00:19:25,306
In a story with so many famous

511
00:19:25,306 --> 00:19:28,255
names, the sources only support a handful

512
00:19:28,255 --> 00:19:29,693
of facts about each,

513
00:19:29,693 --> 00:19:31,995
and we have tried to stay inside

514
00:19:31,995 --> 00:19:32,355
them.

515
00:19:32,535 --> 00:19:35,836
Good stories attract embellishment; we would rather

516
00:19:35,836 --> 00:19:37,649
give you less and have it be

517
00:19:37,649 --> 00:19:38,038
right.

518
00:19:38,388 --> 00:19:40,869
Wikipedia lists the F forty as the

519
00:19:40,869 --> 00:19:43,862
last Ferrari approved by Enzo Ferrari and

520
00:19:43,862 --> 00:19:44,811
the car that,

521
00:19:44,811 --> 00:19:46,052
by many accounts,

522
00:19:46,052 --> 00:19:48,899
set the template for the supercars that

523
00:19:48,899 --> 00:19:49,556
followed.

524
00:19:49,736 --> 00:19:52,060
The sources we read do not make

525
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:54,684
that second claim in so many words,

526
00:19:54,684 --> 00:19:56,633
so we call it our reading:

527
00:19:56,633 --> 00:19:58,883
a stripped-down, turbocharged,

528
00:19:58,883 --> 00:20:02,106
rear-wheel-drive car with a manual gearbox,

529
00:20:02,106 --> 00:20:04,655
built to celebrate an anniversary.

530
00:20:05,006 --> 00:20:08,014
Classic Motorsports calls it very durable,

531
00:20:08,014 --> 00:20:10,091
and cheaper to run than the F

532
00:20:10,091 --> 00:20:10,520
fifty.

533
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:13,821
Sotheby's treats it as the subject of

534
00:20:13,821 --> 00:20:16,436
a six-car list of record sales.

535
00:20:16,616 --> 00:20:19,995
The DK Engineering archive describes the car

536
00:20:19,995 --> 00:20:22,298
as it was sold in the nineteen

537
00:20:22,298 --> 00:20:22,989
nineties.

538
00:20:23,169 --> 00:20:25,964
Each source gives a different slice of

539
00:20:25,964 --> 00:20:26,993
the same life,

540
00:20:26,993 --> 00:20:29,714
from showroom to dealer to auction to

541
00:20:29,714 --> 00:20:30,228
garage.

542
00:20:30,579 --> 00:20:32,659
The numbers, one last time,

543
00:20:32,659 --> 00:20:34,201
with our arithmetic.

544
00:20:34,381 --> 00:20:36,587
Thirteen months of development.

545
00:20:36,767 --> 00:20:38,273
Four hundred planned,

546
00:20:38,273 --> 00:20:41,213
one thousand, three hundred eleven built.

547
00:20:41,393 --> 00:20:43,855
About four hundred thousand dollars new.

548
00:20:44,035 --> 00:20:46,600
A bubble at seven times that.

549
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:50,498
A forty-six percent nominal drop for Mansell's

550
00:20:50,498 --> 00:20:50,821
car.

551
00:20:51,001 --> 00:20:54,557
And, in twenty twenty-five and twenty twenty-six,

552
00:20:54,557 --> 00:20:57,533
sales between roughly two point eight and

553
00:20:57,533 --> 00:21:00,654
five point two million dollars for standard

554
00:21:00,654 --> 00:21:01,380
road cars.

555
00:21:01,730 --> 00:21:03,614
We should say what we cannot tell

556
00:21:03,614 --> 00:21:03,843
you.

557
00:21:04,023 --> 00:21:05,795
We do not have a source for

558
00:21:05,795 --> 00:21:08,487
what Enzo Ferrari thought of the finished

559
00:21:08,487 --> 00:21:10,720
car, how many of the one thousand,

560
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,624
three hundred eleven survive,

561
00:21:12,624 --> 00:21:14,593
